  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1957\n£10.00\n\nLow stock, 3 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1957 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O., D.L. Volume LIX January to December 1957.\n\nPublished 1958 - Sydney Lee (Exeter) Ltd. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' 1957 -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed on December 31st, 1957 -p.6\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List December 31st, 1956 -p.7\n\nBattle Honours Awarded for the Second World War -p.8\n\nInfantry Reorganisation 1957 -p.9\n\nMajor-General M. M. A. R. West, C.B., D.S.O. -p.10\n\nRecords of the First Battallion -p.11\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary -p.14\n\nFirst Battalion Letter -p.23\n\nAddress Given to the Regiment by Lieutenant-Colonel J. A. J. Read, D.S.O., M.C. -p.30\n\nVisit of Major-General C. L. Firbank to First Battalion -p.32\n\nFirst Battalion Records of Sport and Training 1957 -p.34\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.49\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.50\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.54\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.57\n\nRegimental Dinner -p.61\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon (First World War) -p.62\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.63\n\nOperations in Cyprus 1956-57 -p.64\n\nCentenary of the Storming of the Cashmere Gate -p.70\n\nDelhi 1857 (Papers of Lt.-Col. C. K. Crosse) -p.74\n\nTwo New Customs -p.77\n\nThe Security Forces in the Kenya Emergency -p.80\n\nBusman's Holiday in Portugal 1957  -p.93\n\nIn Statuo Pupillaris -p.98\n\nA Tour with the Royal Navy -p.108\n\nThe Unveiling and Dedication of the Light Infantry Window at Strensall -p.112\n\nA Visit to Corunna 1957 -p.113\n\nMemorial Chapel, Royal Military Academy, Sandhurst -p.118\n\nA Visit to Papua and New Guinea -p.119\n\nThe Walls of Ayia Phyla -p. 126\n\nThe View from Limassol 1956-57 -p.129\n\nOld Comrades' Association 1957 -p.138\n\nObituary -p.139\n\nIndex -p.142\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nChildren and War – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre V\n£5.00 Add to cart\nConflict & County\n£5.95 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre I\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
